<title>USA: TABLE - Hayes Microcomputer Q2 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Hayes Microcomputer Q2 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Amounts in 000's)</p>
<p>		   Quarter Ending		   Six Months Ending</p>
<p>	 June 30,  March 31,  June 30,     June 30,     June 30,</p>
<p>	    1997     1997	  1996	   1997	   1996</p>
<p> Revenue   $55,721   $39,176    $68,617	$94,897 $145,584</p>
<p>Net Income (loss)</p>
<p>	     (2,465)   (5,369)	(288)	(7,834)    5,226</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said operating expenses were higher in Q2 due to nonrecurring costs associated with its acquisition of Cardinal Technologies Inc and higher sales and marketing expenses due to the launch of its 56K PC Card modem.</p>
<p>The privately-held, Norcross, Georgia-based company is the largest manufacturer of modems worldwide.</p>
<p>Full name is Hayes Microcomputer Products Inc.</p>
</text>
